[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `grep -c 'enum' c_src/include/lib.h c_src/src/lib.c` -> 0, 0.)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Consequently the "error surface" of this library consists entirely of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m *silent* rejections: input values that do not map to a real hue sector are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m absorbed by branch predicates rather than reported. Those are the rows below.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rows 1-2 are the only structural early exit; rows 3-13 are the silent
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m value-rejection paths; rows 14-17 are the generic C-API boundaries the task
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m requires be covered even though the C does not check them.
